fuxi: 0112 -- restart and the cluster clocks on the ethertype channel

The UDP channel (0110/0111) is deaf on hardware: the host's datagram never shows
up as "FUXI CMD: rx" in the console stream, while the ethertype channel from 0106
answers immediately -- "usb: ue0 up, rx 188 tx 368 frames, 657 events".  A kernel
socket bound to INADDR_ANY on a link that comes up before its address exists is
evidently not receiving here, and that is a rabbit hole; the frame path is proven,
and --jkoo has root, so AF_PACKET costs nothing.  The UDP listener stays in the
tree (it is harmless and the reply peer is now correct) but the loop runs on
ethertype from here.

Two commands move over:

  restart  answers, waits a tick so the frame leaves, then PEHaltRestart: the
           phone resets out of the kernel without anyone touching it.
  cpu      in addition to the PMCCNTR answer, calls the EPSS report, so the
           per-cluster perf state and clock land in the console stream on 5140 --
           readable live, no photo, no reboot.

That combination is what makes the loop self-driving: boot over fastboot, watch
5140, restart over 0x88B5, and the phone is back at the bootloader-visible state
in one command.

Harness: applied=111 skipped=0.
